Complete Git Reference & Nested Project Fix
 1. Git Basics
    A.Create a new repository on the command line
      git init                        # Initialize a new Git repository in the current folder
      git add .                       # Stage the README.md file for commit
      git commit -m "first commit"    # Commit the staged file with a message
      git branch -M main              # Rename the default branch to 'main'
      git remote add origin https://github.com/your-git-user-name/git-repo-name.git  # Add remote repository URL named 'origin'
      git push -u origin main         # Push commits to the remote 'main' branch and set upstream



    B.Push an existing repository from the command line
       git remote add origin //github.com/your-git-user-name/git-repo-name.git  # Link local repo to remote GitHub repository
       git branch -M main    # Rename default branch to 'main'
       git push -u origin main   # Push existing commits to remote and set upstream


     c.Configure User
        git config --global user.name "Your Name"               # Set your Git username globally
        git config --global user.email "youremail@example.com"  # Set your Git email globally
        git config --list                                       # View all Git configuration settings

     D.Basic Workflow
        git add .                 # Stage all changes in the repository for commit
        git commit -m "message"   # Commit staged changes with a descriptive message
        git push origin main      # Push local commits to the remote 'main' branch
        git pull origin main      # Pull latest changes from remote to local repository


